  "summary": "Nintendo Switch Sports is Nintendo's motion-controlled sports collection, released for Switch on 29 April 2022.",
  "body": [
    "Nintendo Switch Sports is Nintendo's motion-controlled sports collection, released for Switch on 29 April 2022. Players use Joy-Con movements to serve, swing, bowl and compete within a shared sporting venue. Tennis and bowling return from the Wii Sports tradition alongside activities such as badminton, volleyball, football and swordplay. The collection makes the basic gesture easy to recognize, then places the contest in its timing and direction. A small movement in the room becomes a visible action that another player can immediately understand and answer.",
    "Each sport translates a different physical idea into a short set of controls. A bowling release, a racket swing or a guarded sword strike has its own timing, while the game handles much of the surrounding movement. Local multiplayer lets those actions form a social contest around one screen, and online matches provide further opponents. The variety makes moving between sports part of the experience: learning the next event begins with finding how a familiar real-world action has been simplified into a useful Joy-Con gesture.",
    "Director Yoshikazu Yamashita led a team that began considering a Switch successor to Wii Sports after the console's release. The venue and new avatars give the collection another visual identity, while continuing updates expanded the sporting selection with golf and later basketball. Haruko Torii and Takuhiro Honda composed the music. The project carries a recognizable Nintendo idea across generations of hardware: a clear physical gesture can introduce a game quickly, while competition and the people sharing the room supply reasons to keep playing."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "The living room becomes a sporting venue",
    "A Joy-Con translates the gesture",
    "A familiar idea in another setting"
  ],
